Design of Experiments: Central Composite Design (CCD) for Parameter Optimization
================================================================================

Experiment Name: Liquidity Risk Parameter Optimization
Design Type: Central Composite Design (Rotatable)
Purpose: Optimize key parameters to minimize liquidity risk while maintaining operational efficiency

Design Parameters:
-----------------
Number of Factors: 5
Number of Center Points: 6
Alpha (axiality): 2.378 (rotatable design for 5 factors)
Total Runs: 54 (32 factorial + 10 axial + 6 center + 6 replicates)

Factor Definitions:
------------------
Factor A: RESERVE_RATIO
  Low Level (-1): 0.05
  High Level (+1): 0.20
  Center (0): 0.125
  Axial Low (-α): 0.0109
  Axial High (+α): 0.2391
  Units: Ratio (fraction of total assets)

Factor B: PAYMENT_ARRIVAL_RATE
  Low Level (-1): 50
  High Level (+1): 200
  Center (0): 125
  Axial Low (-α): 14.33
  Axial High (+α): 235.67
  Units: Payments per hour

Factor C: INTERBANK_CREDIT_LIMIT
  Low Level (-1): 1000000
  High Level (+1): 5000000
  Center (0): 3000000
  Axial Low (-α): 48780
  Axial High (+α): 5951220
  Units: Currency units

Factor D: COLLATERAL_HAIRCUT
  Low Level (-1): 0.10
  High Level (+1): 0.30
  Center (0): 0.20
  Axial Low (-α): 0.0524
  Axial High (+α): 0.3476
  Units: Ratio (fraction of collateral value)

Factor E: QUEUE_PRIORITY_THRESHOLD
  Low Level (-1): 100000
  High Level (+1): 500000
  Center (0): 300000
  Axial Low (-α): 4878
  Axial High (+α): 595122
  Units: Currency units

Response Variables:
------------------
Y1: Average Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR)
  Target: Maximize (optimal ≥ 1.0)
  
Y2: Maximum Queue Length
  Target: Minimize (optimal < 10 payments)
  
Y3: Average Settlement Time
  Target: Minimize (optimal < 5 minutes)
  
Y4: Gridlock Frequency
  Target: Minimize (optimal = 0 events per day)
  
Y5: System Throughput
  Target: Maximize (payments settled per hour)

Run Specifications:
------------------
Randomization: Complete randomization with blocking by day
Replications: 30 per design point
Simulation Length: 8 hours (one business day)
Warm-up Period: 1 hour

